umber of cores and performance",marks:1,command_word:"identify",content:[{type:"text",value:"The specification of two CPUs is shown in Fig. 1."},{type:"table",headers:["Computer 1","Computer 2"],rows:[["Clock Speed: 1 GHz","Clock Speed: 1.4 GHz"],["Cache size: 2 MB","Cache size: 2 MB"],["Number of Cores: 4","Number of Cores: 2"]]},{type:"text",value:"When running a 3D flight simulator, Computer 1 is likely to run faster than Computer 2."},{type:"text",value:"Using the information in Fig. 1, identify one reason for this."}],answer:{guidance:"Correct answer: it has more cores. Accept equivalent answers explaining that Computer 1 can split work across more cores.",marks_breakdown:[{criteria:"More cores identified as the reason",marks:1}]}},{question_id:"2(b)",parent_question:2,topic:"other components affecting performance",marks:2,command_word:"identify",content:[{type:"text",value:"The specification of two CPUs is shown in Fig. 1."},{type:"table",headers:["Computer 1","Computer 2"],rows:[["Clock Speed: 1 GHz","Clock Speed: 1.4 GHz"],["Cache size: 2 MB","Cache size: 2 MB"],["Number of Cores: 4","Number of Cores: 2"]]},{type:"text",value:"Identify two other parts of a computer that are not in Fig. 1, which could improve the performance of the computers."}],answer:{guidance:"1 mark each. Accept RAM, SSD, HDD, or graphics card (GPU). Other appropriate responses such as motherboard or sound card may also be accepted.",marks_breakdown:[{criteria:"First valid computer component identified",marks:1},{criteria:"Second valid computer component identified",marks:1}]}},{question_id:"2(c)",parent_question:2,topic:"cache size and performance",marks:2,command_word:"explain",content:[{type:"text",value:"Explain one reason why the cache size affects the performance of the CPU."}],answer:{guidance:"1 mark for a correct point and 1 mark for the linked explanation. For example: data is transferred faster, which makes the CPU more efficient; or it is faster to transfer data to and from cache than to and from RAM.",marks_breakdown:[{criteria:"Valid point about faster cache access",marks:1},{criteria:"Linked explanation of improved efficiency or comparison with RAM",marks:1}]}}],Z0={paper_id:U0,qualification:W0,component:V0,title:G0,year:Y0,session:K0,total_marks:X0,questions:Q0},ek="J277-TOPIC-1.1.3",tk="J277",ak="TOPIC",rk="Embedded Systems",ik=null,nk=null,sk=10,ok=[{question_id:"1",parent_question:1,topic:"embedded system characteristics",marks:3,command_word:"explain",content:[{type:"text",value:"A car has a 'Follow Me' system that uses a cruise control feature to allow the car to follow the car in front of it."},{type:"text",value:"It will keep the same speed and distance without the driver's intervention. The cruise control system is an example of an embedded system."},{type:"text",value:"Explain the reasons why the 'Follow Me' system is an example of an embedded system."}],answer:{guidance:"1 mark each to max 3. Valid points include: it has a specific purpose / only performs one limited task; it is built within a larger device or car; it has dedicated hardware or sensors; it has a microprocessor; it uses built-in software / firmware / ROM; its operation is hard to change or update; it is an automated control system.",marks_breakdown:[{criteria:"One valid reason linked to embedded-system characteristics",marks:1},{criteria:"Second valid reason",marks:1},{criteria:"Third valid reason",marks:1}]}},{question_id:"2",parent_question:2,topic:"embedded systems in cars",marks:3,command_word:"identify and explain",content:[{type:"text",value:"A car comes with many embedded systems, for example parking sensors."},{type:"text",value:"Identify one other embedded system that could be found in a car and explain why this is an embedded system."},{type:"table",headers:["Example embedded system","Explanation"],rows:[["",""]]}],answer:{guidance:"1 mark for a suitable example such as auto lights, auto window wipers, sat nav / GPS, air conditioning / climate control, radio / infotainment, lane assist, engine management system, auto-park, cruise control, auto-brake, Follow-me, or dashcam. 1 mark each to max 2 for explanation, e.g. limited functions, dedicated microprocessor, or hard to change function. Do not award simply 'built into the car / larger machine' because that is already given in the question.",marks_breakdown:[{criteria:"Valid embedded-system example in a car",marks:1},{criteria:"First valid explanation point",marks:1},{criteria:"Second valid explanation point",marks:1}]}},{question_id:"3",parent_question:3,topic:"embedded systems terminology",marks:4,command_word:"complete",content:[{type:"text",value:"The following paragraph describes embedded systems."},{type:"text",value:"Complete the paragraph by selecting terms from the list and writing them in the correct places. Not all terms are used."},{type:"text",value:"Terms: actuator, applications, change, functions, laptop, larger, lights, microprocessor, processor, range, smaller, washing machine"},{type:"text",value:"Embedded systems have limited _____. They are often built into a _____ machine. Two examples of embedded systems are a _____ and automated _____ in a car."}],answer:{guidance:"1 mark for each completed term. functions; larger; washing machine; lights.",marks_breakdown:[{criteria:"functions",marks:1},{criteria:"larger",marks:1},{criteria:"washing machine",marks:1},{criteria:"lights",marks:1}]}}],ck={paper_id:ek,qualification:tk,component:ak,title:rk,year:ik,session:nk,total_marks:sk,questions:ok},lk="J277-TOPIC-1.2.10",dk="J277",uk="TOPIC",pk="Data storage: Numbers",mk=null,hk=null,fk=10,gk=[{question_id:"1(a)",parent_question:1,topic:"terabytes to megabytes conversion",marks:1,command_word:"identify",content:[{type:"text",value:"Tick one box to identify the quantity of megabytes that is the same as 2 terabytes."},{type:"table",headers:["","2000 MB","20 000 MB","200 000 MB","2 000 000 MB"],rows:[["Select","","","",""]]}],answer:{guidance:"1 mark. Correct answer: 2 000 000 MB.",marks_breakdown:[{criteria:"Correct answer: 2 000 000 MB",marks:1}]}},{question_id:"1(b)",parent_question:1,topic:"denary, binary, and hexadecimal conversion table",marks:4,command_word:"complete",content:[{type:"text",value:"Each row in the table contains a number that is written as a denary value, 8-bit binary value, and a 2-digit hexadecimal value. Some values are missing."},{type:"text",value:"Complete the table by writing in the missing value for each number."},{type:"table",headers:["Denary","8-bit binary","2-digit hexadecimal"],rows:[["38","","26"],["","01001110","4E"],["156","10011100",""],["215","","D7"]]}],answer:{guidance:"1 mark for each completed row. The missing values are 00100110, 78, 9C, and 11010111.",marks_breakdown:[{criteria:"38 = 00100110 = 26",marks:1},{criteria:"78 = 01001110 = 4E",marks:1},{criteria:"156 = 10011100 = 9C",marks:1},{criteria:"215 = 11010111 = D7",marks:1}]}},{question_id:"1(c)",parent_question:1,topic:"binary addition",marks:2,command_word:"complete",content:[{type:"text",value:"Complete the binary addition of these two 8-bit binary numbers: 01110011 + 00110100. Show your working out."}],answer:{guidance:"1 mark for correct working with the carries shown and 1 mark for the correct answer 10100111.",marks_breakdown:[{criteria:"Correct binary working is shown with the required carries",marks:1},{criteria:"Correct answer: 10100111",marks:1}]}},{question_id:"1(d)",parent_question:1,topic:"right binary shift result",marks:1,command_word:"identify",content:[{type:"text",value:"Tick one box to identify the result of a 2-place right binary shift on the binary number 01110111."},{type:"table",headers:["","00011101","11101110","00111011","11011100"],rows:[["Select","","","",""]]}],answer:{guidance:"1 mark. Correct answer: 00011101.",marks_breakdown:[{criteria:"Correct answer: 00011101",marks:1}]}},{question_id:"1(e)",parent_question:1,topic:"binary shift to multiply by 8",marks:2,command_word:"describe",content:[{type:"text",value:"Describe the binary shift that can be used to multiply any number by 8."}],answer:{guidance:"1 mark for identifying a left shift and 1 mark for identifying that the shift is 3 places.",marks_breakdown:[{criteria:"Left shift",marks:1},{criteria:"3 places",marks:1}]}}],_k={paper_id:lk,qualification:dk,component:uk,title:pk,year:mk,session:hk,total_marks:fk,questions:gk},yk="J277-TOPIC-1.2.1",wk="J277",vk="TOPIC",bk="Primary storage (Memory)",kk=null,xk=null,Ak=14,qk=[{question_id:"1(i)",parent_question:1,topic:"need for primary and secondary storage",marks:2,command_word:"explain",content:[{type:"text",value:"An artist has a computer that they use to create images."},{type:"text",value:"Their computer has both hardware and software."},{type:"text",value:"The hardware includes primary and secondary storage."},{type:"text",value:"Explain why a computer needs both primary and secondary storage."}],answer:{guidance:"1 mark each. Primary storage is needed for the active data, instructions, software, or operating system that the processor needs to access. Secondary storage is needed to store files and data long-term or permanently when the power is off.",marks_breakdown:[{criteria:"Primary storage is needed for active data, instructions, software, or start-up access",marks:1},{criteria:"Secondary storage is needed for long-term or permanent storage when the computer is turned off",marks:1}]}},{question_id:"1(ii)",parent_question:1,topic:"secondary storage device and stored data",marks:2,command_word:"give",content:[{type:"text",value:"An artist has a computer that they use to create images."},{type:"text",value:"Give one example of a secondary storage device that the artist's computer will have and an example of the data that will be stored on it."}],answer:{guidance:"1 mark for a valid secondary storage device and 1 mark for a valid example of data stored on it. Devices could include a hard drive, SSD, USB memory stick, flash memory card, CD, or DVD. Example data could include created images, documents, software, files, or data moved from RAM to virtual memory.",marks_breakdown:[{criteria:"A valid secondary storage device is identified",marks:1},{criteria:"A valid example of data stored on that device is given",marks:1}]}},{question_id:"1(iii)",parent_question:1,topic:"virtual memory statements",marks:4,command_word:"complete",content:[{type:"text",value:"The computer has Virtual Memory (VM)."},{type:"text",value:"The table has four statements about VM. Not all of the statements are correct."},{type:"text",value:"Tick the True column for the statements that are correct. Rewrite any statement that is incorrect in the False column by changing the statement to make it true."},{type:"table",headers:["Statement","True","False - rewrite the statement to make it true"],rows:[["A section of primary storage is partitioned to act as virtual memory","",""],["Data from ROM is transferred into VM","",""],["VM is needed when RAM is full, or nearly full","",""],["Data from VM is transferred back to secondary storage when needed","",""]]}],answer:{guidance:"1 mark for each row. Row 1 should be corrected to secondary storage. Row 2 should be corrected to RAM. Row 3 is true. Row 4 should be corrected so data from VM is transferred back to RAM when needed.",marks_breakdown:[{criteria:"Row 1 corrected to secondary storage",marks:1},{criteria:"Row 2 corrected to RAM",marks:1},{criteria:"Row 3 identified as true",marks:1},{criteria:"Row 4 corrected so data is transferred back to RAM",marks:1}]}},{question_id:"2(i)",parent_question:2,topic:"RAM and ROM difference",marks:1,command_word:"state",content:[{type:"text",value:"A smart television allows the user to search the Internet and watch videos online."},{type:"text",value:"A smart television has both RAM and ROM."},{type:"text",value:"State the difference between RAM and ROM."}],answer:{guidance:"1 mark. ROM is non-volatile while RAM is volatile, or ROM usually cannot be changed while RAM can be changed. A valid answer must state both sides of the difference.",marks_breakdown:[{criteria:"A valid two-sided difference between RAM and ROM is stated",marks:1}]}},{question_id:"2(ii)",parent_question:2,topic:"RAM data examples",marks:2,command_word:"give",content:[{type:"text",value:"Give two examples of data that a smart television could store in RAM."}],answer:{guidance:"1 mark each to a maximum of 2. Valid examples include a running web browser or application, parts of the operating system currently running, the current video or programme being watched, buffered data, button presses from the user, current volume, current channel, or the current source such as HDMI1.",marks_breakdown:[{criteria:"One valid example of data currently stored in RAM",marks:1},{criteria:"A second valid example of data currently stored in RAM",marks:1}]}},{question_id:"3",parent_question:3,topic:"RAM and ROM in a sat nav",marks:3,command_word:"identify",content:[{type:"text",value:"A satellite navigation system (Sat Nav) uses RAM and ROM."},{type:"text",value:"Tick one box in each row to show whether each of the statements is true for the RAM or ROM in a Sat Nav."},{type:"table",headers:["Statement","RAM","ROM"],rows:[["Stores the boot up sequence of the Sat Nav.","",""],["The contents are lost when the Sat Nav is turned off.","",""],["Holds copies of open maps and routes.","",""]]}],answer:{guidance:"1 mark for each correct row. The boot up sequence is ROM. Contents lost when the Sat Nav is turned off is RAM. Open maps and routes are RAM.",marks_breakdown:[{criteria:"Boot up sequence identified as ROM",marks:1},{criteria:"Contents lost when turned off identified as RAM",marks:1},{criteria:"Open maps and routes identified as RAM",marks:1}]}}],Ck={paper_id:yk,qualification:wk,component:vk,title:bk,year:kk,session:xk,total_marks:Ak,questions:qk},Sk="J277-TOPIC-1.2.2",Tk="J277",Pk="TOPIC",jk="Secondary storage",Mk=null,Ik=null,Ek=34,Nk=JSON.parse(`[{"question_id":"1","paren