th of 4 is used. This means 4 bits are used to store the colour for each pixel. State the maximum number of different colours that can be represented in 4-bits."}],answer:{guidance:"1 mark. Correct answer: 16.",marks_breakdown:[{criteria:"Correct answer: 16",marks:1}]}},{question_id:"2(iv)",parent_question:2,topic:"effects of increased colour depth",marks:2,command_word:"state",content:[{type:"text",value:"The colour depth is increased to 2 bytes. State two effects that this change can have on the image."}],answer:{guidance:"1 mark each to a maximum of 2. Valid effects include improved image quality, larger file size, or more colours being represented.",marks_breakdown:[{criteria:"One valid effect of increasing colour depth",marks:1},{criteria:"A second valid effect of increasing colour depth",marks:1}]}},{question_id:"3",parent_question:3,topic:"image metadata examples",marks:3,command_word:"identify",content:[{type:"text",value:"A student takes a photograph of their science experiment. The image file includes metadata."},{type:"text",value:"Identify three pieces of metadata that is often stored with an image."}],answer:{guidance:"1 mark each to a maximum of 3. Valid examples include height, width, colour or bit depth, date, geolocation, file size, file type, compression type, and author.",marks_breakdown:[{criteria:"One valid piece of image metadata",marks:1},{criteria:"A second valid piece of image metadata",marks:1},{criteria:"A third valid piece of image metadata",marks:1}]}},{question_id:"4(a)(i)",parent_question:4,topic:"image storage capacity calculation",marks:2,command_word:"calculate",content:[{type:"text",value:"Each image has a fixed size of 1 MB. The storage device has a capacity of 3 GB."},{type:"text",value:"Calculate how many images can be saved on the storage device. Show your working."}],answer:{guidance:"1 mark for correct working and 1 mark for the answer 3000 images.",marks_breakdown:[{criteria:"Correct working is shown, such as 1000 x 3",marks