rk for a second valid LAN-distinguishing reason from the same list (must be a distinct, non-contradictory point).","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"1(b)(i)","parent_question":1,"topic":"mesh topology definition","marks":2,"command_word":"describe","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Describe what is meant by a mesh topology."}],"answer":{"guidance":"1 mark each to max 2. Valid points: (Partial mesh) all devices are connected to one or more devices // (Full mesh) all devices are connected to every other device; No need for central management / switch / device / node // all devices are equal // decentralised; Multiple routes/paths (between devices). MP1 BOD each device is connected to other devices // all devices are connected. MP2 do not accept 'no central server'.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Award 1 mark for one valid mesh-topology characteristic from: (partial mesh) all devices connected to one or more devices, OR (full mesh) all devices connected to every other device (BOD: each device is connected to other devices / all devices are connected); no need for central management/switch/device/node, all devices are equal, decentralised; multiple routes/paths between devices.","marks":1},{"criteria":"Award 1 mark for a second valid mesh-topology characteristic from the same list. Do NOT accept 'no central server' for the decentralised point.","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"1(b)(ii)","parent_question":1,"topic":"mesh vs star topology","marks":4,"command_word":"describe","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Describe one benefit and one drawback of the network using a mesh topology instead of a star topology."},{"type":"text","value":"Benefit Drawback"}],"answer":{"guidance":"each to max 2 for drawback max 2 for benefit e.g. Benefits: No purchase/cost of central switch / device … lower cost to install/maintain network // no need to setup / connect to the central device More connections/paths between devices // alternate routes … no single point of failure // if a connection 