ng the no-switch point; 'if a connection breaks the nodes can still connect' expanding the alternate-routes point). MP3 and MP4 may be in a single statement.","marks":1},{"criteria":"Award 1 mark for a valid drawback of mesh from: large number of/more connections/wires (can involve redundant connections / impractical); reduced central management/control/oversight (less control over transfer/security); less secure (more routes/devices for interception/attack); difficult to find an error (multiple routes); mesh uses more power (more nodes per transmission).","marks":1},{"criteria":"Award 1 mark for a matched expansion or second valid drawback. Do NOT accept faster/slower transmission speeds (these depend on media and other factors).","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"1(c)","parent_question":1,"topic":"cloud storage drawbacks","marks":5,"command_word":"describe","content":[{"type":"text","value":"The youth centre is going to store data about users and events using cloud storage."},{"type":"text","value":"Describe the drawbacks to the youth centre of storing the data on the cloud."}],"answer":{"guidance":"each to max 5 e.g. Can be expensive for large amounts of data / long term / hosting // may be ongoing subscription // no control over changing costs May be limited amount of storage No control over security // Need to rely on provider for security May be hacked/stolen/intercepted/affected by a virus May lose (personal) data // May lose access to data May go against DPA/legislation // Data may be misused (by provider) May not be clear where in the world the data is stored Limited/No control over access Company/cloud could go down No control over backup // May not have (automatic) backups … … data is not retrievable Need internet access // no internet access means no data … access speed depends on network/connection speed Concerns over ownership of the data Need to remember login details // may forget/lose login details Users may need training MP1 needs more than high cost, 