rk for: DNS looks for URL/domain to find matching IP (in a table/database/files/lists). MP3 awarded for the use of the DNS converting URL to IP.","marks":1},{"criteria":"Award 1 mark for: if not found, the request is transferred to a higher-level DNS (accept: another/larger DNS).","marks":1},{"criteria":"Award 1 mark for: DNS returns IP address to computer/browser (do not award 'user' on its own); OR an error is returned/sent if the IP cannot be found.","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"2(i)","parent_question":2,"topic":"star topology diagram","marks":3,"command_word":"draw","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Draw a diagram to show how the five computers, switch and two printers are connected in a star topology. You must include labels."}],"answer":{"guidance":"1 mark each for drawing showing: (1) 5 computers, 2 printers and 1 switch all clearly labelled; (2) all devices directly connected to the switch (or all computers to switch and each printer to a switch/computer); (3) only 8 devices and no additional connections other than to the switch. Allow any type of computer e.g. PC, laptop. Do not accept 'client' for computer. MP1 requires at least 5 computers, at least 2 printers, and at least 1 switch.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Award 1 mark for: 5 computers, 2 printers, and 1 switch all clearly labelled. Allow any computer type (PC, laptop). Do NOT accept 'client' for computer. There must be at least 5 computers, at least 2 printers, and at least 1 switch.","marks":1},{"criteria":"Award 1 mark for: all devices directly connected to the switch (or all computers connected to the switch and each printer to a switch/computer).","marks":1},{"criteria":"Award 1 mark for: only 8 devices and no additional connections other than to the switch (or central device, or printers connected to only one computer each).","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"2(ii)","parent_question":2,"topic":"star vs mesh topology","marks":2,"command_word":"give","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Give one benefit and one drawback of the office using a star topology instead of a mesh topology."},{"type":"text","value":"Benefit Drawback"}],"answer":{"guidance":"for benefit e.g. Easier to add new nodes // easier to setup BOD Central device can monitor/control transmissions Faster data transmission Fewer data collisions One connection/computer breaks the network still works Less cost of cables for drawback e.g. Switch fails the network fails // reliant on a central device (working) // single point of failure Extra cost of central device/switch Speed, cheaper etc. on its own is NE Server is irrelevant. Read whole benefit and award a valid benefit. Read whole drawback and award a valid drawback. Do not award contradictory statements.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Award 1 mark for one valid benefit of star over mesh from: easier to add new nodes / easier to setup (BOD); central device can monitor/control transmissions; faster data transmission; fewer data collisions; if one connection/computer breaks the network still works; less cost of cables. ('Speed', 'cheaper' on their own are NE.)","marks":1},{"criteria":"Award 1 mark for one valid drawback of star vs mesh from: switch/central-device failure brings the network down (single point of failure); extra cost of central device/switch. Do not award contradictory statements.","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"2(iii)","parent_question":2,"topic":"switch role in network","marks":3,"command_word":"describe","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Describe the role of the switch in the star topology."}],"answer":{"guidance":"each to max 3 e.g. Connects the devices together in the network // allows devices to communicate in the network Receives data from (all) devices in the star topology Record/register/store the address of devices connected to it … … in a table Uses MAC address of devices Direct data to destination … if address not recorded transmit to all devices","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Award 1 mark for any one of: connects 