lue":"01 for i = 0 to 4\\n02  empty = 0\\n03  if appointments[i] == \\"\\" then\\n04   empty = empty + 1\\n05  endif\\n06 next i\\n07 print(\\"empty\\")"},{"type":"text","value":"The algorithm contains logic errors.\\n\\nDefine the term logic error."}],"answer":{"guidance":"A logic error is an error that does not cause the program to crash but produces unexpected output.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"An error that does not cause the program to crash // produces unexpected output","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"19(b)(ii)","parent_question":19,"topic":"identify-logic-errors","marks":4,"command_word":"Identify","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Identify the line number of two logic errors in the code above and explain why each is an error."},{"type":"text","value":"Logic error 1"},{"type":"text","value":"Line number ____"},{"type":"text","value":"Explanation ____"},{"type":"text","value":"Logic error 2"},{"type":"text","value":"Line number ____"},{"type":"text","value":"Explanation ____"}],"answer":{"guidance":"Mark in pairs.\\n\\nError 1: Line 02 // empty = 0. Explanation: Will reset empty to 0 on each iteration of the loop.\\n\\nError 2: Line 07 // print(\\"empty\\"). Explanation: Will print out the string \\"empty\\" instead of the value held in the variable.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Line 02 // empty = 0 identified","marks":1},{"criteria":"Will reset empty to 0 on each iteration of the loop","marks":1},{"criteria":"Line 07 // print(\\"empty\\") identified","marks":1},{"criteria":"Will print out the string \\"empty\\" instead of the value held in the variable","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"20(a)(i)","parent_question":20,"topic":"invalid-input-validation","marks":3,"command_word":"Complete","content":[{"type":"text","value":"The program should only allow values from 0 to 300 inclusive as valid inputs. If the data entered breaks this validation rule, an error message is displayed.\\n\\nComplete the following program to output \\"Invalid input\\" if the data 