al = totalMins(hours, minutes)\\nprint(finalTotal)\\nfunction totalMins(hours, minutes)\\n  total = hours * 60 + minutes\\n  return total\\nendfunction\\n\\n1. Parameters named in function must be used within the function itself.\\n2. Does not matter if function uses different names to those declared in main program.\\n3. Return must be included with the correct local variable for total.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Program calls function correctly using hours and minutes variables","marks":1},{"criteria":"Parameters used appropriately","marks":1},{"criteria":"Calculation is computed accurately","marks":1},{"criteria":"Final total is returned suitably","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"20(d)(iii)","parent_question":20,"topic":"flowchart-to-program","marks":4,"command_word":"Rewrite","content":[{"type":"text","value":"The following flowchart outputs a message depending on how long each person has spent playing computer games."},{"type":"image","kind":"diagram","src":"data/png/j277/diagrams/games-time-flowchart.png","alt_text":"Flowchart that outputs one of two messages depending on whether minutes played is greater than 120."},{"type":"text","value":"Rewrite the flowchart as a program.\\n\\nYou must use either:\\n- OCR Exam Reference Language, or\\n- a high-level programming language that you have studied."}],"answer":{"guidance":"Example:\\nminutes = input(\\"Enter minutes played\\")\\nif minutes > 120\\n  print \\"You played games for too long!\\"\\nelse\\n  print \\"You are under your time limit!\\"\\nendif\\n\\nHigh-level programming language / OCR Exam Reference Language response required. Do not accept pseudocode / natural English. Accept alternative (but suitable) output messages. Accept logical comparison of input less than or equal to 120 and appropriate True/False statements.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Takes input from the user","marks":1},{"criteria":"Compares if input is larger than 120","marks":1},{"criteria":"...if true, outputs \\"You played game