mp) is converted to an integer (on the 4th line).","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Convert data to an integer / int (in context)","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"22(a)","parent_question":22,"topic":"flowchart-design","marks":5,"command_word":"Design","response_style":"drawing","content":[{"type":"text","value":"A fast food restaurant offers half-price meals if the customer is a student or has a discount card. The offer is not valid on Saturdays.\\n\\nThe restaurant needs an algorithm designing to help employees work out if a customer can have a half price meal or not. It should:\\n- input required data\\n- decide if the customer is entitled to a discount\\n- output the result of the calculation.\\n\\nDesign the algorithm using a flowchart."}],"answer":{"guidance":"Question asks for a flowchart. Answers as pseudocode, high level language or other forms are not acceptable (NAQ).\\n\\nGuidance for correct outputs:\\n- Not Saturday and (either a student or has a discount card) -> Half price\\n- Saturday or (not a student and doesn\'t have a discount card) -> Full price\\n\\nBP 4 and 5 only to be awarded if all decisions ensure correct output and clear what the decisions are. FT for incorrect shapes used or no inputs as long as decisions are logically correct. Must attempt all three decisions. Allow calculation of half price / full price instead of message but this must still be output. Inputs / decisions may be presented as individual or combined boxes but must still store as three variables.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Start and end/stop with all boxes connected, no orphan boxes","marks":1},{"criteria":"Input three variables using parallelogram shape","marks":1},{"criteria":"Checks all three criteria (day, student, discount card) using diamond shape(s) with two lines from each","marks":1},{"criteria":"Outputs \\"full price\\" with correct conditions using parallelogram shape","marks":1},{"criteria":"Outputs \\"half price\\" with correct conditions using parallelogra