me-teacher-rule","marks":1,"command_word":"State","content":[{"type":"text","value":"The program design is updated to create usernames as follows:\\n- If the person is a teacher, their username is the last 3 letters of their surname and then the first 2 letters of their first name.\\n- If the person is a student, their username is the first 3 letters of their first name and then the first 2 letters of their surname.\\n\\nWhat would be the username for a teacher called Fred Biscuit using the updated process?"}],"answer":{"guidance":"Correct Answer Only (allow any case). Last 3 letters of Biscuit = \'uit\', first 2 letters of Fred = \'Fr\'.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"uitFr","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"23(b)(ii)","parent_question":23,"topic":"username-algorithm","marks":6,"command_word":"Write","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Write an algorithm for the updated program design shown in (i)."}],"answer":{"guidance":"Example:\\nAsk the user to input the data, store in variables firstname, surname and role.\\nCheck whether the role entered is teacher.\\nIf it is, join the right 3 most letters in surname with the left 2 letters in firstname. Store this in username.\\nIf it is not teacher, join the left 3 letters from firstname with the left 2 letters from surname. Store this in username.\\nOutput the value in username.\\n\\n1 mark for each correct bullet to a maximum of 6. If used, a flowchart should represent the bulleted steps in the answer column.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Taking firstname, surname and teacher or student as input","marks":1},{"criteria":"Checking IF role is teacher/student (using appropriate selection)","marks":1},{"criteria":"For teacher: Generating last 3 letters of surname using appropriate string manipulation","marks":1},{"criteria":"...Generating first 2 of letters of firstname and adding to previous","marks":1},{"criteria":"For student: correctly calculating as before","marks":1},{"criteria":"Correct concatenation and output","mark