nly understand machine code","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"7b","parent_question":7,"topic":"compiler vs interpreter differences","marks":4,"command_word":"describe","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Either a compiler or an interpreter can translate the code."},{"type":"text","value":"Describe two differences between how a compiler and an interpreter would translate the code."}],"answer":{"guidance":"1 mark to be awarded for the correct identification and one for a valid description up to a maximum of 4 marks. No more than 2 marks for answers relating only to interpreters and no more than 2 marks for answers only relating to compilers.\\n\\nValid differences: compiler translates all the code in one go whereas an interpreter translates one line at a time; compiler creates an executable whereas an interpreter does not / executes one line at a time; compiler reports errors at the end whereas an interpreter stops when it finds an error.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"First identification of a difference (compiler vs interpreter)","marks":1},{"criteria":"Description/expansion of the first difference","marks":1},{"criteria":"Second identification of a difference (compiler vs interpreter)","marks":1},{"criteria":"Description/expansion of the second difference","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"8i","parent_question":8,"topic":"binary search on grades","marks":4,"command_word":"show","content":[{"type":"text","value":"A school uses a mobile phone app to allow parents to book appointments for parents' evenings. Parents must log in before they can use the system. They then choose to book a new appointment, view all appointments already made or update their personal details. If parents choose to view their appointments, they can either view them on-screen or print them off. Each teacher has the assessment grades for each student. These grades are stored in numerical order."},{"type":"text","value":"The grades for one student are shown:"},{"type":"text","value":"2   3   4   5   6 