her:\\n• OCR Exam Reference Language, or\\n• A high-level programming language that you have studied."}],"answer":{"guidance":"Example:\\ntotal = 0\\ndate = input(\\"Please enter date\\")\\nfor count = 0 to events.length-1\\n  if events[0, count] == date then\\n    total = total + events[3, count]\\n  endif\\nnext count\\nprint(\\"There were \\" + total + \\" events on \\" + date)\\nBP2 loop allow off by one errors, looping to array length or array length - 1. BP4/5 allow array reference as either column major or row major. Only give output mark if attempt made to calculate total within the algorithm. Must be 0 to 6, not 1 to 7.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Input date and store in variable / use directly","marks":1},{"criteria":"Access all seven (indexes 0 to 6) events in array // loop for each event in array","marks":1},{"criteria":"Attempt at selection","marks":1},{"criteria":"...to compare date input against date in array (element 0)","marks":1},{"criteria":"...adding length (element 3) from array to the total if dates match","marks":1},{"criteria":"Outputting calculated total and date in appropriate message(s) at the end","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"8(a)(i)","parent_question":8,"topic":"data types (records)","marks":2,"command_word":"state","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Customers at a hotel can stay between 1 and 5 (inclusive) nights and can choose between a basic room or a premium room. A typical booking record is shown in the table:"},{"type":"table","headers":["Field","Value"],"rows":[["firstName","Amaya"],["surname","Taylor-Ling"],["nights","3"],["room","Premium"],["stayComplete","False"]]},{"type":"text","value":"State the most appropriate data type for the following fields:\\nNights\\nRoom"}],"answer":{"guidance":"Accept other valid data types from high-level languages (e.g. byte, short for integers). Do not accept descriptions (e.g. \\"whole number\\", \\"text\\"). Do not accept \\"character(s)\\" for string.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Ni